  "costUsd": null,
  "content": "Owen's approach play sits below the Division I average on the one measure that has a college figure. It is also below his team on strokes gained.\n\n- **Strokes gained approach:** He loses 4.16 strokes per round over his last ten rounds. That window holds 8 rounds with this stat, from Jun 9 to Sep 26. There is no college figure for strokes gained, so I have no level comparison. The team average is -3.09, and he ranks 6th of 7. The Tour baseline is 0.\n- **Greens in regulation:** He hits 61.11% over 144 holes in the same window. The Division I average is 60%, so he is slightly above it, and he sits 36th percentile among college players over all recorded rounds. The team average is 62.76%, and he ranks 5th of 7. The Tour figure is 66%.\n- **Proximity from 125 to 175 yards:** He averages 50.58 ft over all recorded rounds. The Division I average is 38 ft, so he finishes about 12.6 ft farther from the hole. That puts him at the 22nd percentile among college players. The Tour figure is 30 ft. The team average could not be read.\n\nOwen hits a near-average share of greens, but his approach shots leave him farther from the hole than the Division I average from mid-range. That is where the strokes gained loss shows up. His proximity from other distance bands would show whether the problem is specific to mid-range.",
